hadiths[20]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24356","Ahmad ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abbad ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Ghatafan, from Abu Rafi', who said: We slaughtered a sheep for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he ordered us, and we prepared for him something of its belly, and he ate, then stood and prayed without performing ablution."
"24357","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mukhawwal, from a man, from Abu Rafi', who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to pray with his head tied up."
"24358","Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Khattabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, that Bukayr ibn Abdullah narrated to him, from al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from his grandfather Abu Rafi', who said: Quraysh sent me to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and when I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Islam fell into my heart, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I will not return to them, he said: I do not betray the covenant, nor do I betray goodness, return to them, and if what is now in your heart remains, then return, Bukayr said: And al-Hasan informed me that Abu Rafi' was a Copt."
"24359","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: Abdullah ibn Hasan narrated to me, from some of his family, from Abu Rafi', the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: We went out with Ali when the Messenger of Allah sent him with his banner, and when he drew near the fortress its people came out to him and fought them, and a man of the Jews struck him and threw his shield from his hand, so Ali took a door that was at the fortress and shielded himself with it, and it remained in his hand while he fought until Allah gave him victory, then he cast it from his hand when he finished, and I saw myself among a group with me, seven, I being the eighth of them, striving to turn that door over, and we could not turn it."
"24360","Mu'ammal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Rafi' narrated to me, from his aunt, from Abu Rafi', who said: A roasted sheep was prepared for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and it was brought, so he said to me: O Abu Rafi', hand me the foreleg, so I handed him, then he said: O Abu Rafi', hand me the foreleg, so I handed him, then he said: O Abu Rafi', hand me the foreleg, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, does a sheep have but two forelegs, so he said: Had you been silent, you would have handed me of it whatever I called for, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to like the foreleg."
"24361","Husayn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Abu Rafi', who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sacrificed two white-black castrated rams, and said: One is for whoever witnesses tawhid and his conveying, and the other is for him and his household, so it is as if the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sufficed us."
"24362","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to me, that Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi' narrated to him, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I shall surely know one of you, something of my hadith reaches him while he is reclining on his couch, and he says: I do not find this in the Book of Allah Almighty."
"24363","Affan narrated to us, Hammad informed us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi' informed us, from his aunt Salma, from Abu Rafi', that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went around his wives in one day, washing with this one and with this one, so it was said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you made it one washing, he said: This is purer and better and cleaner."
"24364","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ibn Abi Rafi', who said: Al-Arqam al-Zuhri, or Ibn Abi al-Arqam, who was employed over the charities, passed by me, and sought to take me along, so I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked him about that, so he said: O Abu Rafi', charity is forbidden to Muhammad and to the family of Muhammad, the freedman of a people is from themselves."
"24365","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, said: Husayn ibn Abdullah ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abbas narrated to me, from Ikrimah, who said: Abu Rafi', the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was a boy of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and Islam had entered us, so I embraced Islam, and Umm al-Fadl embraced Islam, and al-Abbas had embraced Islam but he feared his people and concealed his Islam, and Abu Lahab, the enemy of Allah, had stayed back from Badr and sent in his place al-As ibn Hisham ibn al-Mughirah, and likewise they did, no man stayed back but sent a man in his place, then when the good news came to us, Allah suppressed him and disgraced him, and we found strength in ourselves, then he mentioned the hadith."
"24366","And from this place in the book of Ya'qub, mursal with no isnad in it, and he said in it: The brother of Banu Salim ibn Awf said: Among the captives was Abu Wada'ah ibn Subayrah al-Sahmi, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He has in Makkah a clever merchant son with wealth, as if I see him having come to me for the ransom of his father, and Quraysh said: Do not hasten the ransom of your captives, lest Muhammad and his Companions profit against you, so al-Muttalib ibn Abi Wada'ah said: You are right, do so, and he slipped away at night and came to Madinah and took his father for four thousand dirhams and went with him, and Mikraz ibn Hafs ibn al-Akhyaf came for the ransom of Suhayl ibn Amr, and he who had captured him was Malik ibn al-Dukhshun, the brother of Banu Malik ibn Awf."
"24367","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abi Khidash informed me, from al-Fadl ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Rafi', that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abu Rafi', kill every dog in Madinah, so I found some women of the Ansar at al-Sawrayn of al-Baqi' with a dog, and they said: O Abu Rafi', the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has sent our men on a raid, and this dog protects us after Allah, by Allah none can come to us until a woman of us stands between him and it, so mention it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so Abu Rafi' mentioned it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: O Abu Rafi', kill it, for only Allah, mighty and majestic, protects them."
"24368","Aswad ibn Amir and Husayn ibn Muhammad said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from Abu Rafi', from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: When he heard the caller to prayer, he would say like what he says, until when he reached: Come to prayer, come to success, he said: There is no power nor strength but with Allah."
"24369","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Amr, meaning Ibn Abi Amr, from al-Mughirah ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Rafi', the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a shoulder of sheep was brought, and he ate it, then stood to prayer without touching a drop of water."
"24370","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Ghatafan, from Abu Rafi', the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: I slaughtered a sheep for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he ordered me, so I fried for him of its belly, and he ate of it, then stood and prayed without performing ablution."
"24371","Yahya and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, call the adhan in the ears of al-Hasan when Fatimah bore him, with the prayer."
"24372","Abd al-Rahman and Abu Kamil said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Rafi', from his aunt, from Abu Rafi', that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went around his wives together in one day, washing with each one of them, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you not make it one washing, so he said: This is purer and cleaner and better."
"24373","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Amr ibn al-Sharid, that Sa'd bargained with Abu Rafi', or Abu Rafi' bargained with Sa'd, so Abu Rafi' said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The neighbor is most entitled to his saqab, I would not have given you, Abd al-Razzaq said in his hadith: And al-saqab is nearness."
"24374","Muhammad ibn Ja'far and Bahz said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Rafi', that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent a man of Banu Makhzum over charity, and said to Abu Rafi': Accompany me so you may get some of it, he said: No, until I come to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and ask him, so he went to the Prophet and asked him, and he said: Charity is not lawful to us, and the freedman of a people is from themselves."
"24375","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mukhawwal, from Abu Sa'd, who said: I saw Abu Rafi' come to al-Hasan ibn Ali while he was praying, having tied up his hair, so he released it, or forbade him that, and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man praying with his head tied up, so he forbade him, or he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a man to pray while tying up his hair. Abu Kamil narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Mikhwal narrated to us, from Abu Sa'id al-Mu'adhdhin, then he mentioned its meaning, Mikhwal said: from Abu Sa'id al-Madani, then he mentioned its meaning, Abu Ja'far says: O Abu Sa'id, did you see it. Sufyan narrated to us, Salih ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from Sulayman, who said: Abu Rafi' said: He did not order me to bring him down, but his dome was struck and he alighted, Abdullah said: My father said: I asked Ibn Uyaynah about this. Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Let me not find one of you reclining on his couch, a command from my command of what I ordered and forbade comes to him, and he says: We do not know, what we found in the Book of Allah we follow. Zakariya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, who said: I asked Ali ibn Husayn, who said: Abu Rafi', the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed me: That Hasan ibn Ali the elder, when he was born, his mother Fatimah wanted to sacrifice two rams for him, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not sacrifice for him, but shave the hair of his head, then give charity with the weight of his head in silver in the cause of Allah, then Husayn was born after that, and she did likewise. Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Imran ibn Musa narrated to me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father: That he saw Abu Rafi', the freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pass by Hasan ibn Ali while he was praying standing, having fixed his braid in his nape, so Abu Rafi' loosened it, and he turned to him angrily, so Abu Rafi' said: Face your prayer and do not anger, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: That is the portion of Satan, meaning the fixing of his braid."
